    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with an aggressive offensive posture, headlined by **Corbin Carroll** (87.14) and **James Wood** (78.42), our top two projected producers. **Corbin Carroll** is our premier play, benefiting from a pristine matchup against Lorenzen and a significant boost from a high-yield park environment and the favorable #2 spot in the order. Similarly, **James Wood** leverages his elite sprint speed and a prime leadoff opportunity to anchor the outfield; his ability to capitalize on the 4.77 xERA of his opposing starter makes him a foundational piece for our SB-focused strategy. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** (73.28) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) offer high-ceiling upside, with **Mickey Moniak** seeing a massive 14% platoon boost and **Vinnie Pasquantino** gaining additional equity from favorable wind conditions expected to carry the ball out.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Kyle Karros**, who posted a respectable 45.40 but ultimately could not displace the high-efficiency floor provided by our current infield configuration. While **Kyle Karros** benefits from a strong park, his position in the bottom third of the lineup and a neutral platoon matchup against Soroka left him just shy of the threshold needed to crack the active roster. We are maintaining discipline today by benching **Zach McKinstry** as well; despite his versatility, his sub-40 score against a tough matchup makes him a non-starter, preserving our limited game caps for higher-leverage situations.\n\nRisks remain, particularly concerning our middle infield. **Brice Turang** (68.77) holds a strong score, but managers should monitor the \"Wind In\" factor, which threatens to suppress his raw power numbers despite the advantage provided by a slow-working pitcher who is vulnerable to **Brice Turang**\u2019s baserunning profile. We are also tracking the lineups for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Dalton Rushing** closely; while both possess positive indicators against their respective right-handed opponents, their #7 batting positions cap their overall run-scoring potential. With **Jose Caballero** and **Giancarlo Stanton** remaining on the IL, we continue to lean heavily on the speed-at-all-costs philosophy to keep Ghost Ride the WHIP competitive in the 5x5 standings.",
